sentences.l:
But when they were drawn up, each company with its leaders,
the Trojans with clamour and shouting went, like birds,
just as the clamour of cranes is in the heaven, out in front;

which, when they have fled the winter and the immense rain,
with clamour fly toward the streams of Oceanus,
to Pygmy men slaughter and death-fate bringing;

When on a mountain’s peaks the South Wind has poured mist,
to shepherds not at all dear, but to a thief better than night,
so far one sees as one lets fly a stone;

And when they were near, going against one another,
for the Trojans was fighting in front Alexander, godlike-in-form,
a leopard-skin on his shoulders having, and the curved bow
and a sword;

Always for you the heart, like an axe, is unwearied,
which goes through timber under a man who by skill
ship-timber hews out, and increases the man’s rush;
